    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by stolen base upside and favorable SP xERA matchups. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.33) and **Caleb Durbin** (68.14) headline our start list; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits immensely from his leadoff spot and a 14% boost against the platoon, while **Caleb Durbin** exploits a high 5.10 xERA from the opposing arm and the rare opportunity to run against a pitcher with a slow delivery. **Chase Meidroth** (66.48) rounds out the top tier, as his leadoff assignment against Andrew Abbott provides the volume necessary to stabilize our 5x5 categories. Even with the wind blowing in, **Trea Turner** (59.73) remains a lock, as his elite sprint speed against a high-effort delivery profile creates a situational floor that justifies the risk.\n\nThe decision to start **Christian Yelich** (64.13) represents our most aggressive play; despite facing the formidable Roki Sasaki, **Christian Yelich** earns a significant boost from dynamic platoon advantages and a high-likelihood stolen base environment. Conversely, **Pedro Ramirez** (41.74) sits at the bottom of our starting threshold. While his switch-hitting capability keeps him above the benching floor, the difficult matchup against Cade Cavalli makes him the first candidate to be pulled if we reach our game caps early. We are closely monitoring the lineups for **Gary Sanchez**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber**, as their \"Lineup Pending\" status introduces slight volatility to their projected runs and RBI production. With heavy hitters like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Colt Keith**, and **Lars Nootbaar** all unavailable due to team off-days or roster management, we must lean on the speed-first profile of the remaining roster to manufacture the counting stats needed to gain ground in the standings.",
